cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use ASPIR in published work, please cite both the software (this file) and the accompanying article when available."

title: "ASPIR: A Single-Pixel Imaging Research Platform"
abstract: >-
  ASPIR is an open-source desktop application that unifies the complete
  single-pixel imaging computational pipeline behind a graphical user
  interface. It covers dataset generation, mask-pattern design, reconstruction
  with classical and iterative algorithms, post-processing with nine neural
  network architectures, and analysis of reconstruction quality, inference
  latency, and energy consumption. Built-in hardware-backend auto-detection
  enables cross-platform benchmarking across desktop NVIDIA GPUs, Intel CPUs
  (RAPL), and NVIDIA Jetson embedded devices. ASPIR is designed to
  democratise single-pixel imaging experimentation for non-programming
  researchers and to serve as a pedagogical tool for computational imaging,
  compressive sensing, and energy-aware deep learning.

type: software

